### Phase 28: Starter Task Templates API Requests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@ownerToken = YOUR_OWNER_JWT
@userToken = YOUR_AUTHENTICATED_USER_JWT

### 1. Preview starter task templates by category during project creation (any logged-in user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/task-templates?category=Web%20App
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 2. Unknown category falls back gracefully to General
GET {{baseUrl}}/task-templates?category=UnknownCategory
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 3. Create project WITH optional starterTaskKeys (and optional overrides)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "TeamForge Campus Portal",
  "description": "A collaborative student campus portal connecting project owners, contributors, and verified mentors.",
  "requiredSkills": ["React", "Node.js", "TypeScript"],
  "dueDate": "2027-06-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "maxCollaborators": 5,
  "category": "Web App",
  "starterTaskKeys": ["web-repo-readme", "web-main-screens", "web-first-tests"],
  "starterTaskOverrides": {
    "web-repo-readme": {
      "title": "Set up monorepo and onboarding README"
    }
  }
}

### 4. Fetch starter task templates for an existing project (Owner or Admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/task-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 5. Apply starter task templates to an existing project (Owner only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/task-templates/apply
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "keys": ["web-auth-flow", "web-deploy-demo"],
  "overrides": {
    "web-deploy-demo": {
      "title": "Deploy staging preview environment",
      "description": "Publish working staging preview link and verify environment health check endpoint."
    }
  }
}


